@startuml Linkwise_Session_Sequence
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F

actor Operator
participant "AI host" as AI
participant "MCP adapter" as MCP
participant "Use-case service" as APP
participant "Station actor / lease" as ACTOR
participant "Policy engine" as POLICY
participant "Radio adapter" as RADIO
participant "Winlink client" as WL
participant "Modem adapter" as MODEM
participant "PTT arbiter" as PTT
database "Audit / event store" as AUDIT
participant "Independent emergency stop / TX inhibit" as ESTOP

AI -> MCP: prepare(candidate_id, request_context)
MCP -> APP: typed PrepareCandidate
APP -> ACTOR: enqueue exclusive mutation
ACTOR -> POLICY: validate profile, candidate, idle, limits
POLICY --> ACTOR: allow typed config / deny
ACTOR -> RADIO: apply config under lease
RADIO --> ACTOR: supported-field readback
ACTOR -> AUDIT: record decision + requested/readback state
ACTOR --> APP: short-lived PreparedHandle (lease retained)
APP --> MCP: prepared result
MCP --> AI: handle + expiry + state revision

AI -> MCP: start_session(handle)
MCP -> APP: typed StartSession
APP -> ACTOR: adopt lease; revalidate all current state
ACTOR -> POLICY: recheck grant, inventory, config, interlocks
POLICY --> ACTOR: automatically issue bounded grant / reject
ACTOR -> WL: begin supported client session
WL -> MODEM: start modem link
MODEM -> PTT: assert(one-use transmit permit)
PTT -> POLICY: verify lease, session, budget, watchdog
POLICY --> PTT: authorized / reject
PTT --> MODEM: keying state observed
MODEM --> WL: link progress / outcome
WL --> ACTOR: session and transfer events
ACTOR -> PTT: release on completion, abort, timeout, or fault
PTT --> ACTOR: release requested / observed
ACTOR -> AUDIT: append lifecycle and outcome events
ACTOR --> APP: terminal session summary
APP --> MCP: bounded result + outcome distinctions
MCP --> AI: result (not a delivery claim beyond client evidence)

Operator -> ESTOP: activate (only human runtime actuator)
ESTOP -> PTT: independent hardware inhibit / release
ESTOP -> ACTOR: latch E-stop state if software reachable
ACTOR -> WL: abort active client session
ACTOR -> AUDIT: append emergency-stop event

alt validation, readback, or policy failure
  ACTOR -> PTT: idempotent release
  ACTOR -> AUDIT: record denial/fault and unresolved state
  ACTOR --> APP: reject; invalidate handle; release lease as safe
end
note over ESTOP,PTT
Emergency stop bypasses MCP and AI and latches the station safe.
No runtime human reset/approval/control surface is provided.
end note
@enduml
